From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alejandro Garcia <skipper.pelygro@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 22:28:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos: google: gs201-panther: default to
 suspend-to-idle

The firmware advertises PSCI SYSTEM_SUSPEND, so the kernel offers deep
sleep and makes it the default: /sys/power/mem_sleep reads
"s2idle [deep]" on the Pixel 7. Linux has no gs201 sleep sequence yet,
and the phone never wakes from deep. Pass mem_sleep_default=s2idle, as
the Pixel 7 Pro does, so a suspend that names no state stays in s2idle.

Tested on a Pixel 7 from slot B (7.3.0-rc6): /sys/power/mem_sleep reads
"[s2idle] deep".

Suggested-by: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Alejandro Garcia <skipper.pelygro@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-panther.dts | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-panther.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-panther.dts
index fa2d96a76..1c36f6112 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-panther.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-panther.dts
@@ -26,7 +26,7 @@ / {
 
 	chosen {
 		/* ABL requires bootargs to exist; it appends its own after these. */
-		bootargs = "console=tty0 panic=10 clk_ignore_unused pd_ignore_unused rdinit=/init omamobile.ufs-probe";
+		bootargs = "console=tty0 panic=10 clk_ignore_unused pd_ignore_unused rdinit=/init omamobile.ufs-probe mem_sleep_default=s2idle";
 		#address-cells = <2>;
 		#size-cells = <1>;
 		ranges;
